      <div class="lp-faq-list">
        <details class="lp-faq">
          <summary>How do I set it up?</summary>
          <p>
            <a href={`${base}get-started/install-desktop/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Install the app</a> on your machine and add your <a
              href={`${base}connect/models/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">AI provider</a
            >: OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenRouter, or your ChatGPT Plus or Pro plan. <a href={`${base}connect/apps/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Connect your apps</a> (Gmail,
            Slack, Notion, Drive, Calendar) with one sign-in, and save the logins Nod may use on websites. Then ask for something,
            in the app or on <a href={`${base}use/channels/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Telegram</a>. About ten minutes.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq">
          <summary>Which models can I use?</summary>
          <p>
            Any of <a href={`${base}connect/models/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">30+ providers</a>, including OpenAI, Anthropic, Google and OpenRouter, or your ChatGPT
            Plus or Pro plan. You can also run a <a href={`${base}connect/local-models/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">local model</a> through Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM or llama.cpp. A
            local model needs tool calling and a 64,000-token context, and small models are less reliable at the safety check.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq">
          <summary>Is it for work or personal stuff?</summary>
          <p>
            Built for people who run their own work: client calls, follow-ups, invoices, supplier portals. It handles life admin
            too, like a refund or a booking.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq">
          <summary>What does it cost?</summary>
          <p>
            Nod is free to download. Connect an AI service or a supported plan. Provider fees apply, and Nod <a
              href={`${base}use/spending/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">shows estimated model costs in Usage</a
            >.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq">
          <summary>Do I need n8n?</summary>
          <p>
            No, Nod is its own app, made by the team behind <a href={n8n} target="_blank" rel="noopener">n8n</a>. It is
            not the n8n AI Assistant.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq">
          <summary>Which computers?</summary>
          <p>
            Mac with macOS 14 or later, Windows 11 in preview, <a href={`${installGuide}#linux`}>Linux x64 as a Flatpak preview</a>, or <a href={`${base}deploy/self-host/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">your own server</a> for one
            person.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq">
          <summary>Can I use it in Europe?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. Nod runs on your own computer, so it works wherever your computer does, including the EU, the UK and
            Switzerland. Your AI provider's own terms still apply.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq">
          <summary>Where does my data go?</summary>
          <p>
            Nod <a href={`${base}trust/privacy/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">stores your database, files, memory, and saved logins</a> on the computer or server that runs it.
            Model services, apps, and websites receive the data they need for your tasks. App connections use n8n and Composio by default.
            Beyond update checks, n8n receives usage data to improve Nod, which you can turn off anytime in Settings, and whatever you choose to share,
            such as feedback, traces or your email.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq">
          <summary>Does it work when my laptop is closed?</summary>
          <p>
            Nod needs the computer running it to stay on and awake. To keep <a href={`${base}use/schedules/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">schedules</a> running while your laptop is closed,
            run Nod on <a href={`${base}deploy/self-host/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">your own server</a> or a <a href={`${base}deploy/mac-mini/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mac mini</a> that stays on.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq">
          <summary>Can I run it in the cloud?</summary>
          <p>Yes. You can <a href={`${base}deploy/self-host/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">host Nod on your own server</a> for one person. A managed hosted version is on the roadmap.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq">
          <summary>Can it make mistakes?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. Its <a href={`${base}trust/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">safety check</a> is a model's judgement, and Nod is an experiment. That is why it
            asks before actions your request does not cover. <a href={`${base}use/spending/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Usage</a> shows recorded app actions, sign-ins, and model costs.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq">
          <summary>Where can I get help?</summary>
          <p>
            Start with the <a href={base} target="_blank" rel="noopener">docs</a>, which cover setup and the <a href={`${base}deploy/troubleshooting/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
              >common problems</a
            >. If something goes wrong, choose <a href={`${base}use/chat/#send-feedback`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Send feedback</a> in the chat. It goes
            to the Nod team at n8n. You can review the diagnostic report before you send it. For questions and tips from other people using Nod, ask in the
            <a href="https://community.n8n.io/c/n8n-labs/48" target="_blank" rel="noopener">n8n community forum</a>.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>

